==English==

===Etymology===
From {{AGr.}} '''[[Πύθων]]''' (''Python'') the name of the mythological enormous serpent at Delphi slain by Apollo, from '''[[Πυθώ]]''' (''Pytho'') the early name of Delphi, from '''[[πυθώ]]''' (''pytho'') "to rot, to decay".

===Pronunciation===
* {{italbrac|[[RP]]}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθən/}}, {{SAMPA|/paIT@n/}}
* {{italbrac|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθɑːn/}}

===Noun===
'''python''' (''plural'' '''[[pythons]]''')

# A type of large [[constrict]]ing [[snake]].

